  "starterCode": "import pandas as pd\n\ndef pandas_unstack_long_to_wide(records: list, id_col: str, metric_col: str, val_col: str) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Unstack Long to Wide** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndef pandas_unstack_long_to_wide(records: list, id_col: str, metric_col: str, val_col: str) -> dict:\n    df = pd.DataFrame(records)\n    p = df.pivot(index=id_col, columns=metric_col, values=val_col)\n    res = {str(c): [round(float(v), 2) for v in p[c].tolist()] for c in p.columns}\n    res[id_col] = list(p.index)\n    return res\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
